[TITLE] Self-monitoring of an isolated power station
[P1] On a hard-to-reach plateau, a station feeds a clinic with a radio relay, weather instruments and safety lighting The micro-grid includes solar panels, lithium batteries and a small diesel generator. Since the road can remain closed for days, a controller measures voltage, current, temperature and vibration every 200 milliseconds. Detailed data remains in place; only a compressed summary is transmitted when the link is operational Medical and communication equipment is a priority
[P2] On October 18, 2025, a dust storm reduced solar output by 34 percent in fifteen minutes. The temperature of the battery cabinet rose by 8°C, while the inverter fan produced an abnormal vibration. Instead of shutting down the station, the system turned off the secondary heating, reduced some of the lighting and started the rescue group. He identified three possible causes of debris on the panels, a worn-out bearing and increasing resistance in a battery connector.
[P3] After the storm, a head-mounted camera read the license plates and alarm codes, then a local processor matched them to the offline manual. The software required that the entire label remain within a clear margin; it also controlled the overall sharpness and that of the top part A sound command asked to back up if an edge was missing, and four stable images were needed The engineers then confirmed the proposed order to clean the panels, replace the bearing, and then tighten the connector The intervention lasted six minutes without recognizing the uncertainty and leaving the final decision to the operator.
============================================================

